.TH UIVIEW 2
.SH NAME
uiview \- ui(4)'s windows from Rust, views of the program's state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
use uiview::*;

fn app(n: &mut i64) -> impl UiView<i64> + use<> {
	column((
		label(format!("count {n}")),
		button("add one", |n: &mut i64| *n += 1),
	))
}

fn main() {
	uiview::run("count", 0, app).unwrap();
}
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Uiview
is a Rust crate that does for
.IR ui (4)
what Xilem (linebender) does for Masonry's widgets.
A function of the program's state gives a tree of views; after each event
it is called again, and the new tree is compared with the old one
(xilem_core's
.BR View ).
What changed goes to
.I ui
as
.BR ctl 's
lines, those of one event in one write: one transaction.
The widgets and what is only theirs (focus, the text being edited) stay in
.IR ui ;
the program holds its own state and nothing else.
.PP
The views:
.BI label( text ) ,
.BI button( "text, f" ) ,
.BI textbox( "text, f" )
.RI ( f
gets each change;
.BI .on_enter( f )
the text when enter is pressed;
.BI .placeholder( p )\fR),
.BI checkbox( "text, checked, f" ) ,
.BI switch( "on, f" ) ,
.BI select( "options, selected, f" )
.RI ( f
gets the index picked),
.BI divider( vertical ) ,
.BI spinner() ,
.BI slider( "min, max, value, f" ) ,
.BI progress( done )
.RB ( None :
not known),
and those holding others:
.BI column( children ) ,
.BI row( children ) ,
.BI list( children )
(a column that scrolls, widgets only for the children seen: long lists),
.BI grid( columns ", " children )
(row by row, a table),
.BI scroll( child ) ,
.BI sized( child )
with
.BI .width( w )
and
.BI .height( h ) .
Children are a view, a tuple of views, a
.BR Vec ,
an
.BR Option ;
.B AnyUiView
is a view of one of several types, chosen at run time.
.BI .flex( f ) ,
.BI .gap( g ) ,
.BI .align( a )
and
.BI .prop( "key, value" )
set
.IR ui (4)'s
properties.
A callback gets the state,
.B &mut
.IR S ,
and changes it.
.PP
A view is a controlled one: what the user changes comes back as an event,
and if the state then says otherwise, the view's value goes to
.I ui
again (a text box whose callback keeps nothing stays as it was).
.PP
.I Run
starts
.B /bin/ui
in a new window
.RB ( window
in
.IR rio (1)),
mounts its files in a namespace of the program's own
.RB ( rfork (RFNAMEG))
and runs until the window is closed.
.I Run_on
does it in a ui already there,
.BI Ui::open( "srv, mtpt" ) .
.PP
.B Cx
holds what views build; tests on the host use it without
.IR ui :
.BR build ,
.BR Cx::message ,
.BR Cx::rebuild ,
and
.B Cx::take
for the transaction made.
.SS Work elsewhere
.B run_with
.RB ( run_on_with )
gives
.I start
a
.B Proxy
of the state first: its
.BI update( f )
runs
.I f
on the state in the program's loop, from any thread (background work), and
the views follow as after an event (false when the window is gone);
.BI every( "period, f" )
does so every
.I period
(a timer). The events are read on a thread of their own.
